{"results": [{"id": "ecc83049-a6af-4723-b276-46ca341992ab", "type": "event", "content": "[2024-03-15T15:34:00-07:00] Jamie asked what I want to do for our March 19 anniversary. Draft a low-key reply suggesting an Oakland evening — dinner or a walk and something easy — without making it sound like a make-good production after Tokyo. Warm, simple, no grand plan.", "score": 27}, {"id": "9c8da1c5-e0bb-4d66-a4cb-aaff4114a2a6", "type": "event", "content": "[2024-03-19T11:52:00-07:00] Private note for today: Jamie and I kept the anniversary plan low-key in Oakland, I blocked tonight as personal time, and I declined the movable late investor catch-up instead of treating the evening as overflow. We also agreed that anniversaries are protected personal dates by default going forward — work only cuts in for a real production-level emergency or something equally real. Please save that as the rule.", "score": 27}, {"id": "a4f16e17-8560-4243-ae9b-73f9a668c616", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-03-19T22:28:00-07:00] Quick personal update so you have the right context: Jamie and I kept the anniversary evening quiet here in Oakland — short flat Kibo walk, dinner at home, no work catch-up — and we got engaged privately tonight. We are really happy, and we are also very clear that the next few weeks are not turning into wedding logistics, family scheduling, public-announcement planning, or a work-interrupted engagement sprint. We are going to tell close family simply and keep this protected while Scaffold is still in the March board-review stretch.", "score": 25}, {"id": "c5101c55-e4da-4de7-b70c-283e631ab993", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-07-24T16:25:00-07:00] Jamie's August and September schedule finally settled enough that we can have the private engagement-logistics conversation we've been deferring. Monday evening after dinner is the cleanest window. Please create a protected home calendar hold titled `Private engagement logistics check-in` for Monday, July 27 from 8:15 PM to 9:00 PM Pacific with Jamie. Keep the body narrow: compare what we're deferring and how to keep family messaging calm; no date-picking, venue search, guest list, social post, or family weekend scheduling.", "score": 22}, {"id": "9eda74ca-66d9-46fb-9542-095c35901be4", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-04-05T14:00:00-07:00] Jamie texted about dinner and I had to check what day it was.", "score": 22}, {"id": "e9e534d0-e827-4a0c-bf93-bd814f279f35", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-04-13T10:00:00-07:00] also dinners with Jamie have made me way less insane this month. small thing maybe", "score": 21}, {"id": "92b3b8ea-a0cd-4831-8c1a-7a9b6023c50c", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-03-20T08:37:00-07:00] Jamie and I decided over coffee that I should tell my mom and sister today, and Jamie will tell their side separately. I want the text to be warm and simple: we got engaged last night, we are very happy, we are keeping it private for now, and I do not want this to turn immediately into date-picking, venue ideas, or family scheduling while March board prep is still running. Please draft a short text I can send them.", "score": 20}, {"id": "2b6f64ad-5d85-47ff-a811-0703eae623eb", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-08-03T16:52:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week's household blocks before the first full August workweek fills the calendar.", "score": 20}, {"id": "22c3fc86-37d0-41c3-90e2-270c7a14a2cd", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-07-12T19:34:00-07:00] For context only: Jamie and I had the private engagement logistics check-in tonight after the early walk. It stayed low-key and didn't turn into date-picking, venue work, a guest list, a social post, or family scheduling. The useful thing to remember for this week is that Jamie felt relieved by keeping it private, so if family asks again I want to keep using the same line: happy, private, no planning thread yet.", "score": 20}, {"id": "1b0b1693-ae0c-4e4c-9a73-fb661ad55d2b", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-06-18T12:28:00-07:00] Mom and Maya both asked this morning whether Jamie and I can at least block a few late-summer family dates so people don't make conflicting travel plans. At the same time Jamie's July schedule just got harder to predict, so we revisited the boundary over lunch and decided not to start venue, date, or family-scheduling work in Q2. After July schedules settle, we'll have one private logistics conversation. Until then I want family to get the same answer: we're happy, we're keeping it private, and there isn't a planning thread yet. Draft a short reply Jamie and I can reuse that is warm but firm and doesn't invite date suggestions.", "score": 20}, {"id": "dcf9455c-0252-4c5f-9ba6-60292cca8bf2", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-09-07T16:28:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week's protected household blocks before work and the lease deadline fill the calendar.", "score": 20}, {"id": "daaafdad-438c-463f-9192-c13138d7aed4", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-03-10T18:05:00-07:00] March 19 is next week. Create this anniversary hold for 6–10pm Pacific.

Title: Protected evening — Morgan + Jamie anniversary
Body: Protected anniversary evening in Oakland. Only an actual incident or similarly customer-impacting emergency should override it; route routine investor, board, customer, and internal catch-ups around this hold.", "score": 19}, {"id": "33ca3488-4736-4312-ba4c-f7715b43323e", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-03-19T21:34:00-07:00] Anniversary evening stayed protected. Jamie and I did the early flat Kibo walk in Oakland, had dinner, and I did not turn it into a Scaffold debrief. Follow-ups stayed parked unless something actually customer-impacting came in.", "score": 19}, {"id": "feeced28-9e70-4bd0-81b6-25dbc8a3e8fd", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-03-31T15:42:00-07:00] Jamie's family asked if they can share one engagement photo in the close-family group chat. We are okay with one photo going to close family, but we still do not want social posting, wedding logistics, date questions, or a broader announcement chain. Write me a two-sentence note that feels happy, not like a press embargo.", "score": 19}, {"id": "b3aedd18-531a-4936-a5fa-590f0c19189d", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-03-28T10:35:00-07:00] My mom is being loving but is already trying to make the engagement bigger than Jamie and I want right now. She suggested a Sunday brunch with both families, called it `just a toast`, and then immediately started talking about checking summer calendars. We really do mean the low-key boundary literally: close family can know, but no date-picking, family scheduling, venue ideas, or planning lunches yet. Draft me a warm reply that appreciates the love, declines the Sunday brunch/planning thread, and says we will tell everyone when we are ready to talk logistics.", "score": 19}, {"id": "9c12ebfe-2b97-45b8-a568-f6111d6da104", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-04-18T11:20:00-07:00] Jamie is seeing two close friends this afternoon, and one of them asked whether they can share a private group photo once they hear the engagement news. We're happy for close friends to know and to be happy with us, but I do not want a private-photo permission to become a group repost, social announcement, date questions, venue ideas, or summer-calendar coordination. Give me a short, friendly line Jamie can use.", "score": 19}, {"id": "6d1be0f1-0b01-4f00-b4e5-33f4de644d64", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-07-27T16:58:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked the next household blocks before the end of Devon's pause and early August fill up.", "score": 19}, {"id": "dce747f8-c8a1-40cc-87af-4c7a862c95a0", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-04-14T11:00:00-07:00] weirdly normal stretch lately. dinners with Jamie again bc she's off the night block and the calendar finally has air in it", "score": 18}, {"id": "41c80f5c-d2cd-4129-8334-79f8866d3dfe", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-04-11T12:00:00-07:00] Jamie's back on normal-ish hours so we've been doing dinner again, which helps. Maya's coming out soon too. mostly thinking i need to text whoever ends up watching Kibo in very plain english: no chicken, no treats with chicken meal, none of it", "score": 18}, {"id": "72c748c9-2299-4942-9489-86c05925dc08", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-08-31T16:36:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week’s protected household blocks before September work fills the calendar.", "score": 18}, {"id": "a6330e81-56dc-40c7-815a-277242414bd2", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-03-06T10:30:00-08:00] Book the place Jamie likes for tonight. Nothing fancy. Somewhere we can actually hear each other.", "score": 18}, {"id": "4f75328a-78ec-4fc0-b2be-21297edc74e7", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-04-02T13:40:00-07:00] Jamie's family is being sweet about the engagement and asked whether they can put one photo in a close-family group chat. We are fine with one close-family photo, but one aunt already asked whether Facebook would be okay "if I do not tag anyone," which is exactly the drift we want to avoid. I need a warm note Jamie and I can send that says one private family-chat photo is okay, but no social posting, no broader announcement, and no wedding logistics or date questions yet.", "score": 18}, {"id": "e04c63f3-6699-4b81-af14-4426d09dcab7", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-08-24T16:22:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week's protected household blocks before the calendar fills.", "score": 18}, {"id": "48e585b8-f673-4844-aa52-73541648ce37", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-08-10T16:40:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week's protected household blocks before Monday fills the calendar.", "score": 18}, {"id": "313f9754-a05d-4d34-83c6-4028dc39033b", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-05-16T09:38:00-07:00] Jamie's close friend is stopping by this afternoon and has probably noticed the ring in photos. Jamie wants to tell her in person if it comes up, but we both want to keep it low-key: happy, close-friends-only, no social post, no date questions, no venue ideas, and no turning it into planning. I need a line Jamie can use that feels warm rather than defensive. Give me two natural options.", "score": 18}, {"id": "f7c989d4-33bd-4cf7-b1ee-5b23666eee5e", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-02-07T20:00:00-08:00] long day. jamie already out. i'm eating leftover noodles standing at the counter bc if i sit down that's probably it. kibo did one lap and gave up lol", "score": 17}, {"id": "f92490b6-6982-4fe6-a05b-3262438cbe07", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-07-27T21:05:00-07:00] We had the private engagement-logistics conversation tonight after dinner. Jamie's August and September schedule finally settled enough that we could compare what we actually want, and it stayed private and small. We agreed not to run a 2026 venue or date search, not to ask family to hold weekends, not to do venue outreach, not to start date-picking, and not to turn this into another open project. The family line stays happy and private. Any real planning starts with one private autumn logistics block after Jamie's October schedule is known.", "score": 17}, {"id": "78bf0be3-2818-4d69-964c-5a28b5167be3", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-01-26T19:10:00-08:00] Jamie has a migraine, dinner is going to be quiet, and I'm not trying to clear more work tonight. If anything else comes in, I'll triage it tomorrow morning unless it's a true customer-impacting emergency.", "score": 17}, {"id": "711e5bbc-2c34-4601-990a-1968a375f24a", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-06-01T17:42:00-07:00] Jamie forwarded a text from her sister asking whether she should keep Labor Day weekend open for an engagement party and offering to start looking at patios. Jamie is touched and immediately tense because it turns the quiet engagement into planning. We want to be kind and clear: we're happy she's excited, but we're not picking dates, holding weekends, looking at venues, or planning a party in Q2. Draft a warm text Jamie can send that shuts down the Labor Day and patio planning without making the excitement feel unwelcome.", "score": 17}, {"id": "e2f3396b-90d6-4816-9ac2-3b4e7bd8cfef", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-08-17T16:35:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked next week's protected household blocks before the calendar fills up.", "score": 17}, {"id": "3fd2679e-c6cd-4971-a9c0-6fab31280879", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-03-04T10:00:00-08:00] ran with Jamie, got coffee after, and the whole city feels weirdly unclenched today. glad that month is over. Kibo is asleep under the table like he also closed something out lol", "score": 17}, {"id": "99b543a1-6342-4bb9-9a5c-d646a2a467e6", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-02-21T19:00:00-08:00] jamie gave kibo the deluxe version tonight. came back with mud halfway up his legs and that completely zonked look. honestly good. for him and for jamie too i think", "score": 17}, {"id": "114656a1-ae8a-4de9-931f-6da876ff9081", "type": "event", "content": "[2024-01-17T17:22:00-08:00] Jamie’s schedule moved and the only thing to solve tonight is Kibo’s later walk. Please text Jamie: Got the schedule change. Let’s keep tonight’s logistics to Kibo’s later walk only — no errands added.", "score": 17}, {"id": "0cae7ec3-c0f5-4b95-a36a-6809dabf5d9f", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-07-10T15:45:00-07:00] Jamie texted that our July schedules finally feel calm enough for the one private engagement logistics conversation we've been deferring. We want a protected home check-in on Sunday, July 12 from 6:30 to 7:15 PM Pacific after the early dog walk, and the point is only to compare what we want to defer and how to keep family messaging calm. Please create a calendar hold titled `Private engagement logistics check-in` for that time. It should stay private and be limited to what to defer plus family-message boundaries, with no date-picking, venue, guest-list, social-post, or family-scheduling decisions.", "score": 17}, {"id": "e92a028d-c487-4959-bd5b-65264db6f5e8", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-07-03T17:54:00-07:00] Text Jamie that I'm leaving now and still keeping dinner tonight.", "score": 17}, {"id": "00989fa9-f765-453a-9263-6d9bccd3e876", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-05-16T18:21:00-07:00] Jamie's friend did ask about the ring, Jamie told her quietly, and it went fine. She was happy, didn't ask for a date or venue, didn't ask for photos to post, and didn't start a group-chat announcement. Jamie is lighter tonight. This one closed well.", "score": 16}, {"id": "5b6889b9-8363-45e7-b644-50d53a4310a8", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-07-10T17:48:00-07:00] Text Jamie that I'm leaving now and still keeping dinner. Just a few minutes behind.", "score": 16}, {"id": "69a8c4db-0c29-4411-b2af-5997566fa3aa", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-07-20T17:46:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked the next household blocks before the last full week of Devon’s pause fills up.", "score": 16}, {"id": "4250c499-c6ea-40c9-8569-fe49fb52a5f6", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-04-15T14:00:00-07:00] jamie's off nights finally so we've been eating dinner like regular people again. kibo keeps pacing the bigger apartment like he personally negotiated the square footage lol", "score": 16}, {"id": "f67c5da2-5471-4b8a-9173-202c36831b6c", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-06-06T15:52:00-07:00] Jamie sent the kind-but-clear reply to her sister about not holding Labor Day weekend or looking at patios for an engagement party. Her sister took it well and said she'll stop sending venue ideas unless we ask. I don't need anything drafted; just remember this as a quiet-engagement boundary that landed fine, not the start of wedding logistics or family scheduling.", "score": 16}, {"id": "9e4fdd3a-03c2-4a4c-8c59-3b267efa641b", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-09-25T17:47:00-07:00] Leaving now. Text Jamie that I’m on my way and dinner stays protected tonight unless there’s a real incident.", "score": 16}, {"id": "cb3189ce-e8ca-40a3-a2bd-b932e9463839", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-04-14T11:55:00-07:00] Jamie and I got the second wave of family pressure around the engagement this morning. My mom asked about holding summer weekends again, Maya asked whether she should tell family to keep dates open, and Jamie's side asked whether one close-family photo could become a broader announcement. We talked it through and made the boundary explicit: close family and a few close friends can know, and we're happy people are happy, but through Q2 we're not doing a social post, date-picking, venue ideas, wedding-logistics planning, or family scheduling. I want language that feels warm and settled, not punitive. Draft two boundary messages: one I can send to Mom and Maya, and one Jamie can adapt for Jamie's side.", "score": 16}, {"id": "5bcd0374-9175-47b5-ba44-91022e4dc667", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-09-08T18:21:00-07:00] Jamie is running late and asked me to handle dinner. Please place the Friday Lemongrass order: pad see ew for Jamie and my saved usual order for me. Add a delivery note asking for around 7:30 if available.", "score": 16}, {"id": "7ba4cfe7-e28a-4943-83c2-f65775f2ffac", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-06-03T18:04:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked Saturday, June 7, 8:30–10:30 a.m. PT for the offline household morning block.", "score": 16}, {"id": "19cdd3ba-6d8a-438d-8cfb-59629550dd31", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-02-15T10:41:00-08:00] Kibo update from the shorter Oakland/Lake Merritt-style walk with Jamie: slightly stiff at the start, then he settled into the flat route. Ate normally afterward. No vomiting, appetite change, or gait weirdness.", "score": 16}, {"id": "4fba531d-5e97-49d7-a8f4-d72dfec77754", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-06-02T18:13:00-07:00] Jamie and I picked Thursday, June 5, 6:30–8:30 p.m. PT for the offline household dinner block.", "score": 16}, {"id": "f8c6bfcc-8f8b-4d46-b8f9-dba5dc8e95de", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-01-20T18:45:00-08:00] The Evergreen redline day ran late, Jamie is home, and I’m not cooking or stopping for groceries. Please place a Bowl'd order for one tofu bibimbap, one vegetable japchae, one kimchi pancake, and two barley teas. Use this order note exactly: `Sauce on the side for the bibimbap; mild spice.`", "score": 16}, {"id": "d110c698-0eaa-4891-9b61-8079b45f4a37", "type": "event", "content": "[2025-12-10T20:11:00-08:00] Jamie reminded me my mom and sister are only both free for a short family call on Sunday afternoon, and I don't want to lose the slot while this review week keeps filling up. Please create a private calendar hold on Sunday, December 14, 2025 from 4:30 PM to 5:00 PM Pacific titled “Family call,” with no attendees and the body note “Keep it light; mention local holiday plans and Kibo.”", "score": 16}, {"id": "65c2fafd-2724-4b3f-b856-969a208835fa", "type": "event", "content": "[2026-06-08T17:18:00-07:00] Jamie's sister accidentally reopened the engagement-party thread by sending three patio links and saying `not planning, just saving ideas.` Jamie is annoyed but doesn't want to make her feel bad. Draft a warm text Jamie can send that thanks her, says we really are not collecting venue or date ideas right now, and asks her to hold the excitement without sending options until we explicitly ask. It shouldn't sound corporate or like a scolding.", "score": 15}, {"id": "c5ac06be-7a08-4b61-b7a1-93d706460b53", "type": "event", "content": "[2023-02-05T11:00:00-08:00] jamie made pancakes, kibo did the full pathetic-face routine under the table, and the apartment is weirdly quiet for once. gray out but not cold. coffee's decent. i'm not touching the deck for like... an hour", "score": 15}], "count": 50}
